{"author":{"id":"aa05e8c12e0d734c8a7a4c8d0aa648556351b86541dd4c3132d1e0042d98b8af"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1791299766,"nonce":"9lYIqSKUggM4W1XCu3H99MN06k4=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"UCE_lAHOULtcMc8AAAABVEehM87-wTKC","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"404e2cc8ba0fa75b6c8445994e77e24e9a4d82123f84612c80cd4dd67fcdee73"},"target":"60ee4f6c8d899c9fd1b1236ed775635d416f04576f31c2e23af038131a87eb3e","message":"## Github Pages\n\n### pros :\n- simple\n- owned by github : we don't need to manage any infrastructure ourselves\n\n### cons :\n- limited : we can't have any backend if we want to expand the features in the app that would require that\n- owned by github : dependent on github's infrastructure and if there's a problem on their side, there's nothing we can do about it\n\n\n## ENAC pipeline\n\n### pros :\n- flexible : if we need to have a backend for some future features, we can add it without a deployment migration\n- owned by us : we don't depend on any external infrastructure for this app\n\n### cons :\n- we need to manage the deployment layers ourselves\n\n---\n\n## Notes\n- with the currently planned feature set of the app, we are NOT limited by any of the 2 options\n- due to its simplicity, we generally deploy apps like MITSI on github pages","files":null}]}